# Same Settings options on every board (pinned row lists).
# The HackBerry CM5 as it runs (board hackberry-cm5, its desktop unit's environment: APPLAUNCH_SESSION=desktop,
# APPLAUNCH_STD_KEYBOARD=1; at 720x720 the density that matches a board capture, 6.7 px/mm), release.
# expect_rows checks every row of the root menu and of System, in order: a row that appears, disappears or moves on
# one board only fails here (docs/dev/native-settings-page-howto.md section 5: which rows show where, and why). The
# root menu and System must stay the same on every board; only Keyboard test (development builds) and Quit to desktop
# (desktop session) may differ. Review only: no golden.
title settings rows hackberry-cm5 desktop
review
sizes 720x720 640x480
env APPLAUNCH_DEV 0
env APPLAUNCH_BOARD hackberry-cm5
env APPLAUNCH_SESSION desktop
env APPLAUNCH_STD_KEYBOARD 1
@720x720 ppmm 670
apps Settings Store CLI SSH Calculator
clock 20:30
wifi 70
bt on
home
launch Settings
wait 300
expect_rows Screen Wi-Fi Bluetooth Launcher Touch Apps Updates User "Date & Time" System
# System: Up from Screen wraps to the last section
key UP
key ENTER
wait 300
expect_rows Storage Licenses About "Pointer navigation" "SSH indicator" "On-screen keyboard" "Quit to desktop" Reboot Shutdown
# About on every board (also without a board profile): Storage, Licenses, About
key DOWN
key DOWN
key ENTER
wait 300
shot settings_rows_hackberry_about
expect_text Version
expect_text 0.5.0
# the board profile's label second
# branding-allow-begin: the About page's disclaimer line (settings_about_help_model.cpp)
expect_rows "CyberdeckZero Launcher" Board LVGL Version Build Channel Commit "Independent hobby project" "Not affiliated with M5Stack"
# branding-allow-end
key ESC
